## Why This Is Asked
Tests for distributed onboarding require cross-service orchestration, feature flags, and eventual consistency verification beyond typical single-service flows.

## Key Concepts
- End-to-end orchestration across Auth, Billing, and CRM services
- Multi-region latency handling and retry mechanisms
- Data isolation via per-tenant identifiers
- Deterministic mocks for reliable, reproducible tests
- Feature flags to validate multiple code paths in production-like conditions
- Idempotent provisioning to safely handle duplicate events
- Eventual consistency verification across regions

## Code Example
```javascript
// Deterministic mock setup for Playwright routing
page.route('https://auth.example.com/**', route => {
  const tenantId = 'tenant-' + Date.now();
  route.fulfill({
    status: 200,
    body: JSON.stringify({ tenantId, status: 'provisioned' })
  });
});

// Feature flag toggle for onboarding-v2
await context.addInitScript(() => {
  window.__FEATURE_FLAGS__ = { 'onboarding-v2': true };
});

// Retry with exponential backoff for eventual consistency
async function waitForRegionSync(tenantId, region, maxRetries = 5) {
  for (let i = 0; i < maxRetries; i++) {
    const response = await api.get(`/tenants/${tenantId}/status?region=${region}`);
    if (response.status === 'synced') return true;
    await sleep(Math.pow(2, i) * 1000);
  }
  throw new Error('Region sync timeout');
}
```

## Why This Is Asked

Tests for real-time collaboration systems must handle offline edits, eventual consistency, and deterministic merges. This question evaluates your ability to architect an end-to-end flow that exercises offline queues, CRDT-based merging, and version history while ensuring test isolation and reproducibility.

## Key Concepts

- Offline-first collaboration with optimistic UI updates
- CRDT-based merge algorithms ensuring deterministic outcomes
- Test data isolation using per-test seeds and unique identifiers
- Server-sync mocks with controlled timing for deterministic test results

## Code Example

```javascript
// Setup two Playwright contexts for concurrent user simulation
const contextA = await browser.newContext();
const contextB = await browser.newContext();
const pageA = await contextA.newPage();
const pageB = await contextB.newPage();

// Seed a shared base document
const docId = await seedDocument({ content: 'Initial paragraph.' });

// Simulate offline for both users
await setNetworkOffline(pageA);
await setNetworkOffline(pageB);

// User A edits the paragraph
await pageA.goto(`/doc/${docId}`);
await pageA.locator('.editor').fill('User A edited this.');

// User B edits the same paragraph offline
await pageB.goto(`/doc/${docId}`);
await pageB.locator('.editor').fill('User B edited that.');

// Reconnect both users to trigger CRDT sync
await setNetworkOnline(pageA);
await setNetworkOnline(pageB);

// Wait for sync completion
await expect(pageA.locator('.editor')).toHaveText('Expected merged content');
await expect(pageB.locator('.editor')).toHaveText('Expected merged content');

// Verify idempotent replay
const versionBefore = await getDocumentVersion(docId);
await triggerSyncAgain(pageA);
const versionAfter = await getDocumentVersion(docId);
expect(versionAfter).toBe(versionBefore);

// Verify version history
const history = await getVersionHistory(docId);
expect(history).toContain('User A edited this.');
expect(history).toContain('User B edited that.');
```

## Why This Is Asked
This question evaluates the candidate's understanding of end-to-end testing for real-time, distributed systems with regional routing, data consistency, and feature flag safety.

## Key Concepts
- End-to-end testing of event-driven pipelines, cross-region latency, and eventual consistency
- Test data isolation and deterministic environments via mocks and seed data
- Idempotency, replay safety, and rollback semantics for feature flags
- Instrumentation hooks to seed Kafka, mock external feeds, and reset Redis

## Code Example
```javascript
// Playwright test scaffold for the trading alert pipeline
const { test, expect } = require('@playwright/test');

test.describe('Multi-Region Alerting System', () => {
  let kafkaSeeder;
  let redisClient;
  let mockExternalFeed;

  test.beforeEach(async () => {
    // Seed isolated test data per region
    await redisClient.flushdb();
    await kafkaSeeder.seedEvents([
      { region: 'us-east', symbol: 'AAPL', threshold: 150 },
      { region: 'eu-west', symbol: 'BMW', threshold: 85 },
    ]);
    mockExternalFeed.setDeterministicResponse({ AAPL: { price: 152 }, BMW: { price: 87 } });
  });

  test('alerts propagate to correct regional dashboards', async ({ page }) => {
    await page.goto('https://dashboard.trading.example.com');
    await expect(page.locator('.alert').first()).toBeVisible({ timeout: 5000 });

    // Verify cross-region routing
    const alerts = await page.locator('.alert').all();
    expect(alerts).toHaveLength(2);
  });

  test('feature flag rollback triggers correctly', async ({ page }) => {
    await page.goto('https://dashboard.trading.example.com');
    await page.evaluate(() => window.triggerRollback());
    await expect(page.locator('.rollback-success')).toBeVisible();
  });
});
```

